    </title>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Status of Implementation Progress: Output 1: Activities are ongoing. Overall progress towards delivering the output is satisfactory considering start-up delays in implementation. Progress on key activities includes: (i) Capacity Development and Training Plan submitted to the client and approved in Q3 2023; (ii) review of the Corporate Plan (2022-2026) approved in December 2023; (iii) recommendations to improve PVCC&apos;s existing revenue streams has been prepared, identifying significant increase in land tax revenue is possible property valuation methodology, including recommendations to improve PVCC&apos;s existing revenue updated in Q1 2024; (iv) leadership and decision-making training delivered to 58 staff from MOIA and PVCC, 34% of whom are women; and (v) urban planning, development, climate and disaster risk resilience and municipal finance training delivered to 98 government officials, 34% of whom are women.

Output 2: Activities are ongoing. Progress has been affected by delayed implementation of training activities and public awareness campaigns due delayed start-up and subsequent delays in the design of the shelters. Progress to date includes (i) campaign topics defined and schedule developed for six socially inclusive and gender-responsive public awareness campaigns on DRR, climate change assessment (CCA) and the impact of disasters (target is five); (ii) communication firm was engaged to prepare materials for the campaign; and (iii) sub-activities to develop and carry out gender-responsive disaster emergency preparedness plan for the emergency shelters are ongoing and in different phases of completion.

Output 3: Progress on key activities to date includes: (i) a climate and disaster risk assessment completed for Korman shelter, with recommendations made to government on modifications to the shelter design to enhance resilience against climate and geophysical risks; (ii) detailed design of all three shelters were completed and approved (iii) completed the updated safeguards documents (resettlement plan and updated initial environmental examination with environmental management plan) and required environmental clearance/permits; and (iv) completed the procurement of the three shelter packages and signed the contracts with the lowest bid Contractor in September 2024. Construction commenced in November 2024 and is currently ongoing.

Output 4: The output will improve the implementing agency&apos;s capacity to develop, implement, and monitor projects and strengthen PVCC&apos;s capacity to operate and maintain shelters constructed under the project. Activities are still ongoing amidst delays. Draft operations and maintenance plans have been prepared and will be finalized based on the final shelter designs.

Output 5: This output includes coastal protection utilizing nature-based solutions (planting of mangroves) and construction of low rock revetments will be piloted in Fatumaru Bay foreshore. A Coastal Protection Specialist will be recruited to coordinate, manage, and monitor progress and implementation of the nature-based coastal protection pilot activities in Fatumaru Bay.</narrative>
    </title>
